;; #841 NTK (Neural Tangent Kernel) x RLCT -- L3 MeTTa Encoding\n\n;; Type declarations\n(--> ParameterSpace Type)\n(--> Width Nat)\n(--> NTKKernel (-> ParameterSpace ParameterSpace Width Real))\n(--> LossFiber (-> ParameterSpace Width Set))\n(--> RLCT (-> LossFiber Real))\n(--> EffRank (-> NTKKernel Nat))\n(--> GenBound (-> Width Nat Real))\n(--> NTKLoss (-> ParameterSpace Width Real))\n(--> PhaseTransition (-> Width Bool))\n(--> EigenSpectrum (-> NTKKernel (List Real)))\n\n;; D1: Parameter space -- W compact subset R^D, theta in W, d in [1,inf]\n(--> W CompactSubset)\n(--> theta ParameterSpace)\n(--> d Width)\n\n;; D2: NTK kernel map -- K_NTK(x,x2;theta) = inner(grad_theta f(x), grad_theta f(x2))\n(--> K_NTK NTKKernel)\n\n;; D3: NTK-regime loss -- L_NTK(theta;d) = (1/n) sum_i ell(y_i, f_NTK(t;theta,d))\n(--> L_NTK NTKLoss)\n\n;; D4: Loss fiber -- V_eff(d) = {theta in W : L_NTK(theta;d) = L*}\n(--> V_eff LossFiber)\n\n;; D5: Effective rank -- r_eff(K) = (sum lambda_k)^2 / sum lambda_k^2\n(--> r_eff EffRank)\n\n;; D6: Generalization bound -- G(d,n) ~ lambda(d)/n + U(d)/sqrt(n)\n(--> G GenBound)\n(--> U EigenvalueDecayCorrection)\n\n;; D7: Phase transition -- lambda(d) drops from D/2 to lambda_* at d*\n(--> d_star Width)\n(--> lambda_lazy RLCT)\n\n;; C1 PROVEN: R_{an,exp} definability of NTK\n(|- ((==> (--> K_NTK PolynomialInTheta) (--> NTKKernel InRanExp)) (stv 1.0 0.95))\n   ((--> K_NTK PolynomialInTheta) (--> f PolynomialInTheta)))\n\n;; C2 CONJECTURAL: NTK lazy to singular transition\n(|~ ((==> (--> d InfWidth) (--> EffRank Decreasing)) (--> LossFiber Singular)) (stv 0.6 0.7))\n   ((--> SpectralCollapse RankDegeneracy) (--> LossFiber MorseBott))\n\n;; C3 CONJECTURAL: Width as stratum selector\n(|~ ((==> (--> d LargeWidth) (--> LossFiber Morse)) (--> RLCT D/2)) (stv 0.5 0.7))\n   ((--> d SmallWidth) (--> LossFiber MorseBott))\n\n;; C4 CONJECTURAL: Gen bound with NTK correction\n(|~ ((==> (&& (--> n SampleSize) (--> d Width)) (= G lambda(d)/n + U(d)/sqrt(n))) (stv 0.5 0.6))\n   ((--> U EigenvalueDecayCorrection))\n\n;; C5 CONJECTURAL: Phase transition at d*\n(|~ ((==> (= d d_star) (--> RLCT StepDecrease)) (stv 0.5 0.6))\n   ((--> PhaseTransition FeatureLearningEmergence) (--> RLCT Staircase))\n\n;; PLN1: Polynomial gradient implies R_{an,exp} kernel\n(|~ ((Implication (Inheritance NTKKernel PolynomialInTheta) (Inheritance NTKKernel InRanExp)) (stv 1.0 0.95))\n   ((Inheritance K_NTK PolynomialInTheta)))\n\n;; PLN2: R_{an,exp} closure under composition\n(|~ ((Implication (&& (Inheritance K_NTK InRanExp) (Inheritance LossFn InRanExp)) (Inheritance NTKLoss InRanExp)) (stv 1.0 0.9))\n   ((Inheritance SoftmaxCE InRanExp)))\n\n;; PLN3: Eigenvalue collapse to singular fiber\n(|~ ((Implication (Inheritance EffRank Decreasing) (Inheritance LossFiber Singular)) (stv 0.6 0.7))\n   ((Inheritance SpectralCollapse RankDegeneracy)))\n\n;; PLN4: Width filtration monotonicity\n(|~ ((Implication (--> d_ge (>= d2 d1)) (--> RLCT2 (>= RLCT1))) (stv 0.5 0.7))\n   ((--> Width MonotonicStratum)))\n\n;; PLN5: d* scaling from RLCT theory\n(|~ ((Implication (--> d_star (pow n (/ 1 (+ lambda_lazy 1)))) (PhaseTransition d_star)) (stv 0.4 0.6))\n   ((--> RLCTScaling WatanabeBound)))\n\n;; Caveats\n;; 1. C2: NTK eigenvalue collapse to RLCT mapping not formally proven\n;; 2. C3: Width stratum may not be smooth; eigenvalue crossings create non-smooth strata\n;; 3. C4: U(d) eigenvalue correction term ad hoc; tightness not established\n;; 4. C5: d* scaling needs empirical validation; data geometry may affect d*\n;; 5. R_{an,exp} definability assumes polynomial/ReLU activations\n\n;; Cross-references\n;; #9 (Morse-Bott genesis), #77 (lazy regime), #371 (Fast Weight GL(r) fiber), #480 (muP width), #654 (LoRA rank-r), #840 (quantization staircase)\n\n;; Open problems\n;; 1. Is NTK eigenvalue collapse exactly captured by RLCT?\n;; 2. Can d* be predicted from lambda_lazy alone?\n;; 3. How does NTK-RLCT bridge interact with #480 muP?\n;; 4. Does staircase lambda(d) match grokking transitions?\n;; 5. Is NTK-regime fiber Morse for finite d?\n;; 6. Relationship to #77 lazy regime -- same or different?\n;; 7. Does GP limit (d->inf) give lambda->inf or lambda->D/2?\n\n;; Pipeline: L0 COMPLETE, L1 COMPLETE, L2 NOVEL, L3 ENCODED\n;; Next: L4 summary, L5 catalog append